	},
	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Eastern Plaguelands are the dead heart of what was once {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. Here the plague of undeath fell first and hardest, and here it has never lifted. The forests are grey and hung with rot. The rivers run slow and foul. The farms and hamlets that once fed the great city of {red:stratholme}Stratholme{/red} are empty, or worse than empty, for their people still walk the roads in the service of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. No king rules these lands. The Scourge holds them, the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} contests them from the fortress of {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link}, and a small band of the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} keeps a single lamp burning at {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope Chapel{/link} in the far east.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Before the plague, the eastern marches of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} were rich and quiet country. Stratholme was the second city of the kingdom, and around it lay farmsteads, mills and villages such as {link:darrowshire}Darrowshire{/link}, {link:northdale}Northdale{/link} and {link:corin-s-crossing}Corin's Crossing{/link}. {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link} guarded the south-eastern coast. In the north, beyond the {link:thondroril-river}Thondroril{/link} and the forests, the realm of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} kept its border lodges, and the high elves who hunted there were neighbours and friends. No chronicle records when the first of these villages was founded. What is written is how they ended.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The land is a battlefield without a front. The {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} raises its dark temples at {link:corin-s-crossing}Corin's Crossing{/link} and in the {link:plaguewood}Plaguewood{/link}, where the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} builds and stitches new servants. Plaguebats blacken the skies, plaguehounds hunt the roads, and the carrion grubs grow fat on the dead. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} holds {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link} and sends its patrols north toward Stratholme, killing all who do not wear its colours. Against all of this stands {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope Chapel{/link}, where {link:lord-maxwell-tyrosus}Lord Maxwell Tyrosus{/link} and the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} accept any ally, living or dead, who will fight the Scourge. The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} have their own champion here. {link:nathanos-blightcaller}Nathanos Blightcaller{/link} keeps the {link:the-marris-stead}Marris Stead{/link} in the south-west and hunts both the Scourge and the living. And in a hut by the western river lives an old man who was once a paladin of the Silver Hand, {link:tirion-fordring}Tirion Fordring{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.{/b} Ghouls, abominations, gargoyles and the risen dead of the eastern villages fill the land. They serve the Lich King through the necromancers of the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}.
• {b}The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}.{/b} Its knights and clerics hold {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link} and the Scarlet Basilica. They wage war on the Scourge and on everyone else.
• {b}The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link}.{/b} From {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope Chapel{/link} its knights, scholars and quartermasters wage a patient war on the undead, and they reward anyone who brings them the proofs of the fight.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} {link:nathanos-blightcaller}Nathanos Blightcaller{/link}, the champion of {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Banshee Queen{/link}, keeps his own war from the {link:the-marris-stead}Marris Stead{/link}.
• {b}The high elves of {link:quel-lithien-lodge}Quel'Lithien{/link}.{/b} At a lodge on the northern border, rangers of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} still keep their watch.
• {b}The Mossflayer trolls.{/b} From the ruined city of {link:zul-mashar}Zul'Mashar{/link}, a tribe of {link:trolls}forest trolls{/link} fights to survive. The plague has already found some of them.
• {b}The dead who do not rest.{/b} Ghosts walk in {link:darrowshire}Darrowshire{/link} and in {link:terrordale}Terrordale{/link}, and some of them still wait for the living to come home.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Plague.{/b} The {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} spread the plague of undeath through {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}'s grain. The eastern villages ate it and died, and then they rose.
• {b}The Culling of Stratholme.{/b} Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} put Stratholme to the sword rather than let its tainted people rise, and the city burned. The {link:culling-of-stratholme}Culling of Stratholme{/link} is remembered in these lands as the day the east was lost.
• {b}The Fall of Lordaeron.{/b} After the prince returned from the north as a death knight, the kingdom fell. In the {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}, the eastern villages were overrun one by one. At {link:darrowshire}Darrowshire{/link} the defenders made a stand that the Annals of Darrowshire still remember.
• {b}The Wars of the Dead.{/b} The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} made the east its fortress. The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} rose from the survivors and took {link:tyr-s-hand}Tyr's Hand{/link}. The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} broke from the Crusade and found its home at {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope Chapel{/link}. The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} came east when {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Banshee Queen{/link} went looking for one of her old rangers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Plaguelands",
			text = [=[• The folk of {link:light-s-hope-chapel}Light's Hope{/link} say that little {link:pamela-redpath}Pamela Redpath{/link} still waits in her house south of {link:darrowshire}Darrowshire{/link}, and that on quiet nights she can be heard asking travellers for her doll.
• Those who pass through {link:terrordale}Terrordale{/link} speak of a merchant there whose prices, by his own account, are insane. They are not sure the word is only a boast.
• The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} pays in valor for the Scourgestones carried by the dead. Its quartermasters keep careful count.
• It is said that the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} champion at the {link:the-marris-stead}Marris Stead{/link} calls every living servant who comes to him an imbecile, and that this is his kindest word.]=],
		},
	},
})

